"The prognosis is influenced by several documented factors. Favorable findings include a low preoperative PSA of 2.11, a low surgical grade (Gleason 3+3, ISUP grade group 1), negative surgical margins (0.0), and no invasion of the seminal vesicles (0.0). The absence of lymphovascular invasion is also a positive finding. Countervailing factors include the lack of nodal sampling, as no lymph nodes were removed, which widens uncertainty regarding nodal status. Furthermore, the biopsy report lacks a Gleason pattern and ISUP report, which limits the certainty regarding the initial tumor characteristics. The postoperative PSA trajectory and subsequent follow-up are currently unknown, which is a significant factor in the overall prognosis. Information regarding postoperative PSA and its trajectory would be crucial to revise this assessment. The fixed estimated horizon is 76.08 months. This represents expected follow-up without an event, not a known recurrence date. The sensitivity range is 49.45–102.71 months; its coverage has not been validated."
